{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And by the breath of Your nostrils.</b> Like וּמֵרוּחַ אַפּוֹ יִכְלוּ (Job 4:9). You rebuked the waters and they congealed." "<b>The waters piled up.</b> Like עֲרֵמַת חִטִּים (Song of Songs 7:3)." "<b>Like a heap of flowing waters.</b> And the waters, whose nature is to flow and descend, stood like a heap (נֵד), like קָמוּ נֵד אֶחָד (Joshua 3:16), like a wall." "<b>The deeps froze.</b> Congealed, like וְקָפְאוֹן (Zechariah 14:6)." "<b>In the heart of the sea.</b> In the middle of the body, opposite the width of the body."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:43.659049517Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}